 ## Installation
 
+This fork adds Windows and Linux support to [mattt/lore-swift](https://github.com/mattt/lore-swift).
+On Windows, first run `python Scripts/fetch-windows.py`. It verifies the official
+Lore 0.12.0 SDK archive's SHA-256 and extracts the headers, import library, DLL and
+license notices to `Vendor/windows`. `LORE_WINDOWS_SDK_PATH` selects another SDK
+directory. Put that directory on `PATH` when running tests, and ship `lore.dll`
+beside your executable. The runtime itself does not need a Lore CLI installation.
+
+On Linux, run `python3 Scripts/fetch-linux.py`, then add `Vendor/linux` to
+`LD_LIBRARY_PATH` when running tests or your application. The fetcher selects the
+ordinary x86_64 or ARM64 release for the host, verifies SHA-256 and ELF architecture,
+and stages the matching public header. `LORE_LINUX_SDK_PATH` selects another SDK
+directory. Ship `liblore.so` and its notices with your executable.
+
+Windows and Linux use the native C SDK instead of an XCFramework. Pin this package by
+**commit revision** when consuming it: SwiftPM permits the native SDK search flags
+for revision-pinned dependencies. macOS keeps the original XCFramework path.
+
+The binding normalizes C enum signedness at API boundaries because Clang imports
+MSVC enums as `Int32` and Darwin enums as `UInt32`.
+
